# Line endings are pinned, not left to core.autocrlf.
#
# Why this file exists: the [2026-09-19] blob-sink incident. `LocalBlobSink`
# and `S3BlobSink` stored different bytes for identical input, on Windows
# only, because text-mode writes translate newlines and byte-mode writes do
# not. The generator side is fixed. This closes the same class on the git
# side, where it would otherwise reappear on a fresh clone.
#
# This machine has core.autocrlf=true and, before this file, no .gitattributes
# — so the working tree was genuinely mixed: generators/_common.py checked out
# CRLF while docs/decisions.md was LF. Git normalized on commit, so the repo
# stayed consistent and `git status` stayed clean, which is exactly why the
# inconsistency was invisible.

# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
# `eol=lf` is the half that core.autocrlf would otherwise override.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Data files are an interface, not source. A CSV or JSONL that Auto Loader,
# Spark or a Delta reader consumes must have the same bytes on every machine,
# so these are never eol-translated even if a future .gitattributes relaxes
# the rule above.
*.csv   text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.avsc  text eol=lf

# Genuinely binary — never touch.
*.parquet binary
*.zip     binary
*.png     binary

# Power BI Desktop is the editor of the PBIP project (since S23) and rewrites every file it owns with
# CRLF on each save. Its files are pinned to CRLF in the working tree, so the disk matches what Desktop
# writes; the repository still stores LF (git converts on commit), so a diff stays a real diff and a
# fresh checkout on CI is LF as everywhere else. Our own files under powerbi/ (answer_key.sql,
# build_pages.py) are not listed and stay LF. tests/test_line_endings.py keeps eol=crlf inside
# powerbi/ only (Session 31).
powerbi/**/*.json      text eol=crlf
powerbi/**/*.tmdl      text eol=crlf
powerbi/**/*.pbip      text eol=crlf
powerbi/**/*.pbir      text eol=crlf
powerbi/**/*.pbism     text eol=crlf
powerbi/**/.platform   text eol=crlf
powerbi/.gitignore     text eol=crlf
